course: dictionary
lesson: 7320
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. The word plague is a good example. «After the plague so many workers had died that survivors could ask for higher pay.» Here the clues are workers dying and survivors, so plague is a serious disease that spreads quickly and kills many people.
explain: «Pharaoh refused again and again, ten plagues struck Egypt.» Here plague means a disaster sent to punish a land. The story of the ten plagues is in the Bible. Plague can also mean a huge, annoying number of things, as in "a plague of wasps" on a summer picnic.
explain: To plague someone means to keep bothering or troubling them. If your little brother keeps asking the same question all afternoon, he is plaguing you. Check each meaning by putting it into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
fact: A plague is a serious disease that spreads quickly and kills many people.
fact: "The plague" usually means bubonic plague, the Black Death of the Middle Ages, which spread by fleas on rats.
fact: «In 1347 ships from the Black Sea brought a deadly plague to Europe.» Within a few years it killed perhaps a third to a half of all the people.
fact: A plague of something is a huge, annoying number of it, such as «a plague of locusts».
fact: To plague someone is to keep bothering or troubling them. Plague is caused by bacteria and can now be treated with antibiotics.
exercise: «In 1347 ships from the Black Sea brought a deadly plague to Europe.» What does plague mean here? | A ship that carries goods across the sea | *A serious disease that spreads quickly and kills many people | A bad mood that lasts all day | A huge, annoying number of wasps
exercise: «The garden was plagued by weeds all summer.» What does plagued mean? | *Kept bothered or troubled | Cleaned very carefully | Painted in bright colours | Given a lovely present
exercise: Ben says, «Avoid it like the plague!» What does he mean? | *Stay right away from it | Keep it safe in a box | Find it as quickly as you can | Share it with everyone at the party
test: «Ten plagues struck Egypt» in the Bible story. What does plague mean here? | A wet and grey day | A new kind of boat | *Disasters sent by God to punish Egypt | A kind of bird that sings at night
test: Which is a true fact about the plague in the Middle Ages? | *It was spread by fleas on rats | It was spread by eating apples | It only ever affected children | It was cured by sunshine
exam: «After the plague so many workers had died that survivors could ask for higher pay.» Why could the survivors ask for higher pay? | The plague had made the land cheaper to buy | Workers had invented a faster way to farm | The king gave every worker a holiday | *Many workers had died, so workers were scarce
